meta {
  name: Delete an account and everything it owns
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

delete {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/admin/accounts/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{id}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  Trips, traces, points, shortcuts, badges, friendships, group memberships, shared routes, circle places and dashboard keys all go with it — every table referencing the account cascades. Removing the rider from Keycloak is a separate act; doing only that leaves their data here, and doing only this leaves them able to sign in and start again.

  Responses:
  - 204: No Content
  - 400: An administrator cannot delete their own account.
  - 404: Not Found
}
